    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\n\nRuns before the controller method body. On failure \u2192 **HTTP 400** (`ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n3. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (must contain a non-space char)\n4. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n5. **postcode** *(optional)* \u2014 `@Pattern(^\\d{4}$)`\n6. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(^[-+()\\d ]+$)`\n7. **email** *(optional)* \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapping side-effects (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, MapStruct)\n\nAs the DTO populates the `Owner` entity, the **entity setters normalize values**:\n\n8. **address** \u2192 `AddressNormalizer.normalize` (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST/RD/AVE)\n9. **telephone** \u2192 `E164.toE164` \u2014 converts to E.164; **throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 HTTP 400** if not 8\u201315 digits or a known country code has the wrong national length\n10. **email** \u2192 lower-cased\n11. **registrationDate** \u2192 defaults to today (`LocalDate.now()`, 2026-09-04) if absent, then `BusinessDay.rollForward` (weekend \u2192 Monday)\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller body checks & side-effects (execution order)\n\nEach check re-reads all owners via `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (called 7\u00d7, separate read transactions):\n\n12. **`Postcode.isValidForCity(city, postcode)`** \u2192 **HTTP 400** if the 4-digit postcode is outside the city's regional range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099)\n13. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.rejectIfAtLimit`** \u2192 **HTTP 429** if \u2265100 owners already carry today's (business-day) registration date\n14. **`BulkSignup.isWarning`** \u2192 *not a rejection* \u2014 computes a boolean (true if >80 owners share today's date), stashed for the response\n15. **`CityAtCapacityException.rejectIfAtCapacity`** \u2192 **HTTP 409** if \u226550 owners share the normalized city\n16. **`IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate`** \u2192 **HTTP 409** (`DuplicateTelephoneException`) if the identity key `telephone|email|` matches an existing owner (household component always empty)\n17. **`CustomerCode.assign`** \u2192 *side-effect*: sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, NNNN = per-city sequence\n18. **`Namesakes.count`** \u2192 *side-effect*: sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive)\n19. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2192 `@Transactional` `ownerRepository.save` (Spring Data JPA persist; DB IDENTITY-generated id)\n20. **AUDIT log** \u2192 SLF4J logger named `\"AUDIT\"` emits id / customerCode / registrationDate\n21. **Response mapping** (`toOwnerDto`) computes derived fields (displayName, initials, householdId, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference, identityKey), sets `bulkSignupWarning` (from step 14), sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header \u2192 **201 Created**\n\nAlso gating the whole call: **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 authorization runs before everything above.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\nSeveral duplicate/tier facilities exist with wired-up exception handlers but are **never called** in this path, so they apply *no* validation despite appearing to:\n- `DuplicateHouseholdException` (lastName+address dup) \u2014 not invoked; the request's **`sharesHousehold` field is bound but read nowhere**\n- `DuplicateEmailException` (standalone email dup) \u2014 not invoked; a duplicate email is only rejected when telephone *also* matches (via `IdentityKey`)\n- `GoldTier.qualifies` \u2014 not invoked; `membershipLevel` is instead computed inline in the mapper\n\nAnd there are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks, no Spring Data auditing, no event publishing, and no password encoding in the owner-create path."
